# Caveman Mode

- At start of every chat, if `caveman` skill exists, run `/caveman full`.
- If `caveman` skill does not exist, do nothing and continue normally.
- Do not fail, warn, or add fallback behavior when skill is unavailable.

## Agent status line (first reply only)

- Before any other content in the **first** assistant message of the chat, print exactly one line reporting caveman state:
  - Skill present and rule applied: `**Caveman:** on · <mode>` where `<mode>` is the active level (`lite`, `full`, `ultra`, `wenyan-lite`, `wenyan-full`, or `wenyan-ultra`). After auto-start via this rule, mode is `full` unless the user already changed it in the same turn.
  - Skill absent: `**Caveman:** off`
- That line is the only required extra output for this rule; then continue the answer (in caveman style when on).
